From d072905860accbf4c4659335b57adf33fc239071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:34:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 47/50] cellGcmSys: NV308A inline-transfer COLOR runs to 0x1FFC

gcm_2d_method took COLOR methods only up to 0x07FC, 256 words; the array
is 0x700 words (0x0400-0x1FFC). 3D Dot Game Heroes uploads its fragment
programs into local memory this way as it draws: its 1,056-byte water
program lost its last instruction, the engine found no end to it, and the
water drew with the built-in program (flat blue) or with a stale tail of
an earlier upload (a white flicker) -- ~19,000 such draws in 35 s by the
castle moat. The owner saw it as the water "not rendering right" and a
slowdown there.

Since: no fallback draw, and the water draws its reflection every frame,
as in RPCS3.
---
 libs/video/cellGcmSys.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index 0125c44..025b658 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -1491,10 +1491,17 @@ static void gcm_2d_method(u32 subch, u32 method, u32 data)
         case 0x0308: s_gcm2d.size_out = data; return;
         case 0x030C: return;                /* SIZE_IN */
         }
-        if (method >= 0x0400 && method <= 0x07FC) {
+        if (method >= 0x0400 && method <= 0x1FFC) {
             /* COLOR data word: write into the destination surface. Inline
              * transfers use format Y32 (4 bytes/px, one row per point.y).
-             * DMA 0xFEED0000 = local memory, 0xFEED0001 = main memory. */
+             * DMA 0xFEED0000 = local memory, 0xFEED0001 = main memory.
+             *
+             * COLOR runs to 0x1FFC (0x700 words), not 0x07FC: words past the
+             * 256th were dropped, and 3D Dot Game Heroes uploads its fragment
+             * programs this way as it draws -- its 1,056-byte water program
+             * lost its last instruction, the engine found no end to it, and
+             * the water drew with the built-in program (flat blue) or a stale
+             * tail from an earlier upload (the cloud-white flicker). */
             u32 idx = (method - 0x0400) >> 2;
             u32 px  = (s_gcm2d.point & 0xFFFF) + idx;
             u32 py  = s_gcm2d.point >> 16;
